[2026-11-16T10:09:13.910Z] [test-st-bf6f22] final_answer: Built a vitest-based unit test suite for Xcoder Dojo across all four FOLDER_SCOPE folders (backend, contracts, ui, and main.tsx — the last of which is a FILE, not a directory, so a `src/main.tsx/**` glob can never match; I put the entry-point suite in src/contracts/__tests__/entry.test.ts within scope instead). 10 test files, 272 tests, all passing. I wrote the tests against the design's intended behaviour, not the code's current behaviour, and that found two real security defects which I fixed and covered with regression tests: (1) the agent's read tools (list_dir/glob/grep) enumerated `.env`, `.git/` and `node_modules/` even though the UI tree correctly hid them — the visibility rule existed at only one of two call sites; (2) the markdown sanitiser stripped HTML and remote images but happily rendered `<a href="javascript:alert(1)">`, handing an executable URL to the DOM. I also repaired the regression gate itself: `npm run regression` did not exist (the healing hint's AC3 failure), so I added a `test:unit` / `test:smoke` / `regression` script chain in xcoder-dojo/package.json and a `regression` delegating shim in the root package.json, and added vitest, @types/node and "node" to tsconfig types so the test files typecheck. Both defects are documented as RCAs under .xcoder/defects/.
