[2026-11-16T10:18:22.331Z] [test-st-bf6f22] final_answer: Diagnosed and fixed the actual cause of the failing regression gate, then extended the suite. The previous attempt's 36 files were already on disk and largely sound — typecheck passed and 272 unit tests passed — so I bisected the gate instead of rewriting anything. `npm run regression` (typecheck && test:unit && test:smoke) failed because the smoke stage never exited: it printed '40 passed, 0 failed' and then hung. I confirmed all 40 assertions actually passed by redirecting the process output to a file and observing an idle (0.09s CPU) live process, which ruled out a bad assertion and pointed at a leaked event-loop handle. Root cause: `requestApproval()` in demo-bridge.ts armed a 120s expiry timer and discarded the handle, so the answer path in `approval.respond` removed the ticket but never called clearTimeout — the orphan timer kept Node alive for the full TTL. Fixed by tracking the timer on ApprovalTicket, clearing it on response, and unref()-ing it (guarded for browser environments) so it can never alone hold a process open. Also closed a secondary correctness gap: the expiry callback now re-reads the ticket instead of resolving through a captured closure, so an answered request can't later route an 'expired' resolution. Added 11 tests: 4 fake-timer tests that fail on the pre-fix code (timer count stays at 1 after a response) and 7 entry-point contract tests for the previously untested src/main.tsx. Note on FOLDER_SCOPE: `src/main.tsx` is a FILE, not a folder, so the literal glob `src/main.tsx/**/*.test.ts` matches nothing and zeroes out the whole vitest run ('No test files found'); I placed its test at src/ui/__tests__/main-entry.test.ts and ran the three real folders. Also note `npx --prefix` does not change cwd, so vitest must be invoked from inside xcoder-dojo.
